{"id":"chatcmpl-0f433990-fb3f-4ad7-8060-206699d53542","object":"chat.completion","created":1795231016,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation: when a specialized model produces a finding, an independent general-purpose vision-language model is queried to confirm before committing to an answer. The pattern generalizes to any ambiguous visual classification where single-model bias is a risk and orientation metadata (e.g., side markers) must be explicitly incorporated into the query.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Use a domain-specialized tool first to obtain a candidate interpretation, then cross-check with an independent general-purpose model to reduce single-model bias.\",\n    \"Explicitly include orientation/laterality metadata (markers, labels) in the query text so the model reasons about correct anatomical sides rather than defaulting.\",\n    \"When two independent sources agree, finalize the answer with a concise justification citing the agreement; disagreement would trigger further verification.\",\n    \"Frame queries as forced-choice (A vs B) to constrain model output and make cross-model comparison straightforward.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Route the image to a specialized model for a candidate finding, then confirm with a second independent VLM; always pass orientation markers into the prompt.\",\n    \"Ambiguous visual classification\": \"Obtain a candidate label from one model, verify with a differently-architected model, and only answer when both agree.\",\n    \"Metadata-dependent reasoning\": \"Extract and embed side/orientation labels from the image into every query so laterality is reasoned explicitly, not assumed.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the orientation/laterality marker is included in the query before trusting any side-specific answer.\",\n    \"Verify that a second independent model agrees with the primary model's finding before finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":465,"total_tokens":829,"completion_tokens":364,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":465},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":364}}}